23 0 obj
<< /A 316 0 R /Alt (Diagram A shows two gene construct maps for TRV1 and TRV2 T-DNA with labeled genetic elements. Image B displays a young green seedling in soil at thirteen days post-inoculation. Image C presents a larger plant with mottled leaves at thirty days post-inoculation. Graph D is a bar chart of somatic editing frequency percentages for five PDS target loci, each bar labeled with a value between seventy-nine percent and ninety-five percent. Image E depicts a plant at twenty-seven days with arrows indicating growth points. Image F shows a mature plant at sixty-six days with partially white, variegated leaves. Image G presents another mature plant at sixty-six days with green, healthy-looking leaves and visible fruits. Image H includes two rows showing five green fruits and corresponding outer husks on a black background.) /K 0 /P 8 0 R /Pg 17 0 R /S /Figure /T () >>
endobj
24 0 obj
<< /A 317 0 R /Alt (Panel A shows a green seedling with broad leaves, while panel B displays a white flower with some pink coloration at the center. Panel C presents a table detailing seedling color, plant name, and genotype for multiple samples, showing comparisons between green and white seedlings with corresponding genetic mutation percentages. Panel D is a bar chart labeled \215Genotype frequency in M1 lines,\216 comparing germination rates and genotype frequencies across several plant samples, using colors to differentiate wild type and various mutant genotypes, with a legend indicating each genotype.) /K 0 /P 8 0 R /Pg 18 0 R /S /Figure /T () >>
endobj
25 0 obj
<< /A 318 0 R /Alt (Panel A displays a bar chart comparing somatic editing frequency percentages for sgRNA3, sgRNA4, and sgRNA5 targeting CLV1, showing mean values with error bars. Panels B and C are photographs of CLV1-P1 and CLV1-P2 plants at forty days post-inoculation, with arrows highlighting growth features. Panel D shows a CLV1-P1 plant at sixty-seven days post-inoculation exhibiting mature foliage. Panel E depicts a CLV1-P2 plant at one hundred twelve days post-inoculation bearing multiple green husk fruits. Panel F presents three close-up images of flowers exhibiting varied petal coloration and patterning. Panel G displays three dissected husk fruits arranged to show segment numbers from four to nine. Panel H features a bar chart indicating percentages of edited progeny in populations P1, P2, and P3 with color codes for different genotypes.) /K 0 /P 8 0 R /Pg 19 0 R /S /Figure /T () >>
endobj
